      "issue_number": 63,
      "body": "<!-- corgispec:feature:v1 key=0278b383657b8c7e5345145d2b0c103640d79983db46494c11e0cf81c0dda367 delivery=RFC-0008-simplify-instrument-dependent-apis/S-06-bind-market-state-construction -->\n\n## RFC Slice\n\nRFC-0008-simplify-instrument-dependent-apis/S-06-bind-market-state-construction\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC-022 [automated]: Each of the eight market-state construction modes has one direct operation with an empty\n- AC-023 [automated]: Instrument economics exposes an immutable instrument-bound market-state scope covering\n- AC-024 [automated]: Characterization and property tests prove identical conversion derivation, validation\n- AC-025 [automated]: Completed-artifact fixtures reuse one scope across anchor and rate construction, reject\n\n<!-- corgispec:task-dashboard:start -->\n## Task Dashboard\n\n7/7 tasks complete · 1/1 groups approved\n\n| Group | Name | Status | Tasks |\n|---:|---|---|---:|\n| 1 | Consolidate and bind market-state construction | done | 7/7 |\n\n### Group 1: Consolidate and bind market-state construction\n- [x] 1.1 Add baseline characterization in `MarketStateInstrumentScopeSuite` for the current eight direct modes, omitted/explicit-empty/non-empty conversions, exact public state observations, and complete ordered `MarketStateViolations`; verify with `instrumentEconomics/test` before changing production implementations (AC-022, AC-024).\n- [x] 1.2 Consolidate the eight overload pairs in `Market.scala` into one direct operation each with `additional = Vector.empty`, preserving parameter names, shared validation, and typed calculation; verify the baseline tests and one direct definition per mode (AC-022, AC-024).\n- [x] 1.3 Add the final field-only `MarketState.InstrumentScope`, exact aliases, singleton-returning `forInstrument` factory, and eight one-call delegates; verify exact instrument-dependent input/result assignments, all eight mode results, and default/explicit additional conversions with focused scope tests (AC-023, AC-024).\n- [x] 1.4 Complete scoped/direct characterization and `EconomicsPropertiesSuite` laws for rational anchor/rate coherence, supported foreign identity/lineage rejection, price-grid boundary preservation, invalid anchors, additional conversion order/duplicates, first-error projection, independent state allocation, and concurrent scope reuse; verify all instrument-economics tests pass with independently specified expected results (AC-023, AC-024).\n- [x] 1.5 Add runnable `MarketStateScopeClient.scala` and independently valid `MarketStateScopeMismatch.scala` fixtures under `economics-core-compiler`, wiring them through `EconomicsCompilerBoundarySuite`'s core-only classpath; verify all eight direct/scoped modes and vector argument forms compile without repeated dimensions, each incompatible price/rate/conversion fails at its intended expression, and existing dependency/ownership checks pass (AC-022, AC-023, AC-025).\n- [x] 1.6 Add `MarketStateConstructionBenchmark` in the existing benchmarks module comparing direct and reused-scope construction with empty/non-empty conversions; verify JMH compilation and record representative timing/allocation, host JDK and release target, while source review confirms no new traversal, cached result, shared coordination, or dependency (AC-025 and the RFC-wide allocation risk).\n- [x] 1.7 Run formatting, clean aggregate tests, benchmark compilation/measurement, both reflection-policy scripts, strict readiness, `git diff --check`, and the automated Task Group review loop against the complete diff; resolve actionable findings within the accepted contract and retain the checks/review evidence before this group's dedicated commit and canonical acknowledgement (AC-022–AC-025).\n<!-- corgispec:checkpoint:v3 run=run-4874b9a2-be9a-4d0d-8a20-b391ae7a185b group=1 key=34e5087393241c0c35cdd813a83b805ee080b2d6c55b2883324b19b57caaba3e -->\n<!-- corgispec:task-dashboard:end -->\n",
